# BLOCKED — no fixture serves an erroring transcript
#
# docs/TESTING-HARNESS.md §5 lists `error-mid-stream.json` among the starter transcripts, and
# `crates/fleet-harness/transcripts/error-mid-stream.json` exists, but the `agents` preset
# embeds exactly two documents — `two-turns.json` for Claude and `edit-approval.json` for Codex
# (`crates/fleet-harness/src/fixture/plan.rs::agents`) — and neither ever errors. There are only
# two providers, so a third transcript has nowhere to live, and the frozen `fixture:` vocabulary
# has no sixth preset. A scenario cannot reach a mid-stream error today.
#
# The cheapest fix, for the `scripted-agent` stage that owns the transcripts: give Claude's
# `two-turns.json` a third turn that fails, so the third message a scenario sends errors:
#
#     { "type": "text",  "text": "Checking the lockfile now.", "pace_ms": 10 },
#     { "type": "error", "message": "Selected model is at capacity. Please try a different model." },
#     { "type": "end_turn", "status": "failed" }
#
# A transcript's exhausted turns answer with an empty, cleanly completed turn
# (`agent/transcript.rs::next_turn`), so the two existing turns keep their meaning and only the
# third one changes. `Settlement::Failed` is Claude's `result/error_during_execution`.
#
# The assertions below are written against `Attention::Failed`, which the projection reports as
# the thread state `failed`; they have never been run, because nothing can produce that state.
fixture: agents
await idle
key o
await screen == Workspace 20000

key ctrl-s a
await agents.threads[0].provider == claude 20000
click agents.composer
type what does this crate do
key enter
await agents.threads[0].state == working 20000
await agents.threads[0].state == idle 40000

click agents.composer
type and what is the binary called
key enter
await agents.threads[0].state == working 20000
await agents.threads[0].state == idle 40000

# The third turn streams one line and then the provider fails mid-stream.
click agents.composer
type and what does it depend on
key enter
await agents.threads[0].state == failed 40000
assert lists.tabs.selected.marks[0] == failed && agents.threads[0].pending_gate absent
shot failed
dump failed
quit
